# Algorithm

1. Start.
2. Create a binary tree with the given nodes.
3. Traverse the tree level by level using a queue.
4. Check whether any child is present after a missing child position.
5. If a violation is found, display the first violating position.
6. Check completeness using array indices.
7. Compare the results of both methods.
8. Display whether the binary tree is complete or not.
9. Stop.
